# A HiSLIP session as the instrument's state machine sees it, with no sockets. `> sync TYPE CTL PARAM "payload"` is a message from the
# client on the synchronous channel, `> async ...` one on the asynchronous channel; the `<` lines after it are exactly the frames that
# come back, in order (none: nothing). CTL is decimal, PARAM hexadecimal (a MessageID, normally), the payload a quoted string with
# \n, \" and \\ escapes. `@ connect` is a new session. {version} is this crate's version.

# Queries are answered in one DataEND with the MessageID of the query; a client that has read everything sets RMT-delivered (CTL 1).
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF00 "*IDN?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF00 "ferrofire,rtu-1,0,{version}\n"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF02 "MEAS:SCAL:LEVEL?;:MEAS:BIN:ALARM?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF02 "12.5;1\n"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF04 "*CLS"

# A message in pieces is one message: it runs at the DataEND.
> sync DATA 1 FFFFFF06 "*ID"
> sync DATA 1 FFFFFF06 "N?;*OP"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF06 "C?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF06 "ferrofire,rtu-1,0,{version};1\n"

# The status byte on the asynchronous channel: MAV while the last response has not been read.
> async ASYNC_STATUS_QUERY 0 FFFFFF06 ""
< ASYNC_STATUS_RESPONSE 16 0 ""
> async ASYNC_STATUS_QUERY 1 FFFFFF06 ""
< ASYNC_STATUS_RESPONSE 0 0 ""

# -410 Query INTERRUPTED: a message started (RMT-delivered clear) over a response nobody read. The Interrupted names the lost response.
> sync DATA_END 0 FFFFFF08 "*OPC?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF08 "1\n"
> sync DATA_END 0 FFFFFF0A "*OPC?"
< INTERRUPTED 0 FFFFFF08 ""
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF0A "1\n"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF0C "SYST:ERR?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF0C "-410,\"Query INTERRUPTED\"\n"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF0E "SYST:ERR?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF0E "0,\"No error\"\n"

# -420 Query UNTERMINATED: a message that never got its DataEND is given up when another starts; the query in it is not run.
> sync DATA 1 FFFFFF10 "*IDN?"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF12 "SYST:ERR?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF12 "-420,\"Query UNTERMINATED\"\n"
> sync DATA 1 FFFFFF14 "*ESE 7"
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF16 "*ESE?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF16 "0\n"

# The maximum message size of the client cuts a response into frames (272 bytes until it says; the payload is 16 less).
> async ASYNC_MAX_SIZE 0 0 "\0\0\0\0\0\0\0\x40"
< ASYNC_MAX_SIZE_RESPONSE 0 0 "\0\0\0\0\0\x10\0\0"

# Device clear: the async request is acknowledged, the sync channel drops messages until DeviceClearComplete, and no error is raised.
> sync DATA 1 FFFFFF18 "*IDN?"
> async ASYNC_DEVICE_CLEAR 0 0 ""
< ASYNC_DEVICE_CLEAR_ACK 0 0 ""
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF1A "*IDN?"
> sync DEVICE_CLEAR_COMPLETE 0 0 ""
< DEVICE_CLEAR_ACK 0 0 ""
> sync DATA_END 1 FFFFFF00 "SYST:ERR:COUN?"
< DATA_END 0 FFFFFF00 "0\n"

# Messages the server does not know are an Error, not the end; remote/local is accepted.
> sync ASYNC_LOCK 0 0 ""
< ERROR 1 0 "unrecognized message type"
> async DATA 0 0 ""
< ERROR 1 0 "unrecognized message type"
> async ASYNC_REMOTE_LOCAL 3 FFFFFF00 ""
< ASYNC_REMOTE_LOCAL_RESPONSE 0 0 ""
